Whenever a consumer reporting agency prepares a consumer report it shall follow reasonable procedures to assure the maximum possible accuracy of the information concerning the individual about whom the report relates.

I also asked your bureau to provide me with the description of the reinvestigation according to 15 USC 1681i ( 7 ) : ( 7 ) Description of reinvestigation procedure.

A consumer reporting agency shall provide a consumer with a description referred to in paragraph ( 6 ) ( B ) ( iii ) by not later than 15 days after receiving a request from the consumer for that description. 

Equifax indicated that the public record was obtained by a third-party vendor XXXX. XXXX sent me a letter stating that the Bankruptcy item was removed on XX/XX/XXXX Case # XXXX, so how is their reinvestigation valid? 

