8960271,2024-05-08,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I am writing to address several concerning issues regarding the handling of my personal information as governed by various sections of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and related statutes.

Firstly, according to 15 USC 1681 section 602 ( a ) of the FCRA, it is imperative that consumer reporting agencies such as Equifax and XXXX conduct their operations with fairness, impartiality, and respect for consumers ' privacy rights. As a consumer, I am entitled to ensure that my private information remains secure, as reinforced by 15 USC 6801, which mandates financial institutions to uphold the privacy and confidentiality of customers ' nonpublic personal information.

Under 15 USC 1681 section 604 ( a ) ( 2 ), it is explicitly stated that consumer reporting agencies may only furnish consumer reports under circumstances outlined in written instructions from the consumer. I have not provided consent, neither written nor implied, for Equifax, or any furnisher of information to credit agencies to share my personal information.

Furthermore, according to 15 USC 6802 ( b ) ( c ), financial institutions are prohibited from disclosing nonpublic personal information to third parties without informing consumers of their right to opt out of such disclosure. I have not been properly informed of this right by the relevant financial institution.

Additionally, the reporting of adverse items of information, such as the account in question, without my consent violates 15 USC 1681C ( a ) ( 5 ), which restricts consumer reporting agencies from including such information in consumer reports.

Moreover, 15 U.S. Code 1681s2 ( a ) ( 1 ) prohibits the furnishing of inaccurate information to consumer reporting agencies, and Equifax and XXXX are failing to uphold reasonable procedures to prevent violations of the FCRA, as mandated by 15 U.S. Code 1681e.

Finally, under 12 CFR 1016.7, I am exercising my right to opt out of your reporting services effective immediately.

In light of these violations and discrepancies, I expect immediate action to rectify the situation and ensure compliance with all relevant laws and regulations.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",CA,92236,,Web,2024-05-08,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
8960305,2024-05-08,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Trouble with how payments are being handled,"On XX/XX/year>, I opened my Mohela account to make a first payment after having finished school in XXXX XXXX XXXX. I have unsubsidized loans so acknowledge that some interest would be accumulating. When I opened my Mohela account the total cost I owed was {$13000.00}, and I put {$3000.00} down, later receiving an email from Mohela that it had been received and would be processed in 2-3 business days. Once three days passed, I found that {$3000.00} was taken from my bank account, but not deducted from my loan total. I called Mohela and the rep told me that sometimes the first payment takes a little bit longer to process, that they have my money, but that it should be deducted in 10-20 business days, and to keep making payments as usual. Eighteen days later, on XX/XX/XXXX, I went to make another payment, and my total had gone up to {$14000.00}, a total of {$360.00} in interest, which made no sense. I went ahead and paid {$1100.00} toward my loan through Mohela 's website, and again got an email that it had been received and would be processed within 2-3 business days. Two days later, {$1100.00} was taken from my bank account and was taken from my total loan amount listed on Mohela 's website. On XX/XX/year>, I called Mohela regarding my first payment, that it still had not been processed, however, my much smaller payment had been processed and deducted. After being on the phone for nearly an hour, the rep told me that they still had my money, and due to some changes, it could take a total of XXXX business days from my initial payment, pushing the date to as late as XX/XX/XXXX. I accepted that answer, but later decided I wanted a legitimate reason why they couldn't put my {$3000.00} into my Mohela account, but could subtract my {$1100.00} from my loan total, not to mention the fact that they had already told me twice that they