8996680,2024-05-13,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Report provided to employer without your written authorization,"Dear XXXX, Experian, and XXXX, Its vital that we work together to underscore the importance of adhering to rules outlined under 15 U.S.C 1681b ( c ) ( 1 ) ( A ) ( B ) ( i ) ( 3 ). These regulations clearly establish when a consumer reporting agency can furnish a report in connection to credit or insurance transactions that are not initiated by the consumer. 

The law states that reports related to such transactions can only be provided under specific circumstances : ( A ) The consumer explicitly authorizes the agency to provide the report. This authorization must reflect the consumer 's informed consent, underscoring the need for transparent communications. 

or ( B ) If the transaction comprises an unambiguous offer of credit or insurance, even without the initiation of the consumer. 

Further, it's critical to note that, with the only exception provided under section 1681g ( a ) ( 5 ), a reporting agency should never furnish a record of inquiries related to non-consumer initiated credit or insurance transactions. 

By holding firm to these legislated conditions, we ensure that consumers ' rights to privacy and control over their personal information are respected, and trust in our financial system is maintained. It's an essential responsibility, and together, we can ensure that these regulations are upheld for the benefit of all consumers. 

