9054295,2024-05-21,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) 15 USC 1681 section XXXX ( a ), consumer reporting agencies are mandated to perform their duties with fairness, impartiality, and a deep respect for consumer privacy rights. As a consumer reporting agency, Equifax is obligated to protect my private information. This critical responsibility is underscored by 15 USC 6801, which asserts that each financial institution has an ongoing duty to respect the privacy of its customers and to safeguard the security and confidentiality of their nonpublic personal information. 

Entities that provide information to credit agencies, classified as financial institutions under this law, must adhere to 15 USC 1681 section XXXX ( a ) ( XXXX ). This section clearly states that consumer reporting agencies can only furnish consumer reports under specific circumstances, primarily with written instructions from the consumer. Equifax, along with the furnishers of information to credit agencies, does not have my explicit consent to share my personal information. Any previous consent, whether explicit or implied, is hereby revoked and considered null and void. 

